```

### Example 2: Model without timestamps
```
/command create-prisma-model ServiceCategory --includeTimestamps=false
```

### Example 3: Custom table name
```
/command create-prisma-model DeliveryStaff --tableName=delivery_staffs
```

### Example 4: Complete order model
```
/command create-prisma-model Order --fields="mart_id:String,customer_id:String,order_status:String,total_amount:Decimal,is_per_unit_piece:Boolean"
```

## Common Prisma Field Types

```prisma
// Basic Types
field_name    String      // Text
field_name    Int         // Integer
field_name    Float       // Floating point
field_name    Boolean     // True/False
field_name    DateTime    // Date and time
field_name    Decimal     @db.Decimal(10, 2)  // Precise decimals
field_name    Json        // JSON data

// Modifiers
field_name    String?     // Optional (nullable)
field_name    String      @unique  // Unique constraint
field_name    String      @default("value")  // Default value
field_name    DateTime    @default(now())  // Current timestamp
field_name    DateTime    @updatedAt  // Auto-update on change

// Relations
customer_id   String
customer      Customer    @relation(fields: [customer_id], references: [customer_id])

// Arrays
tags          String[]    // Array of strings
items         OrderItem[] // One-to-many relation

// Enums
status        OrderStatus // Enum type (define separately)
```

## Migration Commands

```bash
# Create migration (dev)
npm run migrate:dev

# Apply migrations (production)
npm run migrate:deploy

# Reset database (dev only)
npm run migrate:reset

# Generate Prisma Client
npm run prisma:generate

# View database in Prisma Studio
npm run prisma:studio

# Format schema
npx prisma format

# Validate schema
npx prisma validate
```
